WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.572
OpenAI's new flagship costs twenty

00:00:02.372 --> 00:00:04.402
percent less, but it leaves

00:00:04.202 --> 00:00:05.938
known problems out of its

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.548
own reports twice as often.

00:00:08.248 --> 00:00:09.869
In OpenAI's own test,

00:00:09.669 --> 00:00:11.739
Astra hit a known problem,

00:00:11.539 --> 00:00:13.234
like a missing file,

00:00:13.034 --> 00:00:14.281
and left it out of

00:00:14.081 --> 00:00:16.150
its report in about twenty-two

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.272
percent of trials.

00:00:17.312 --> 00:00:19.577
That is double GPT-6 Astra.

00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:22.232
Astra now costs eight dollars

00:00:22.032 --> 00:00:24.060
per million input tokens and

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.888
forty per million output,

00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:27.335
down from ten and fifty.

00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:29.139
Sol, the everyday model,

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:30.139
stays at two and ten.

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:32.987
Both are OpenAI's first models

00:00:32.787 --> 00:00:35.588
rated Critical for cyber capability.

00:00:35.628 --> 00:00:37.778
Astra turned known Chrome bugs

00:00:37.578 --> 00:00:40.327
into working code execution fifty-three

00:00:40.127 --> 00:00:41.901
point five percent of the

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:44.225
time, up from thirty-one point five.

00:00:44.775 --> 00:00:46.336
So the defaults are tighter.

00:00:46.376 --> 00:00:48.456
The models refuse more dual-use

00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:50.626
requests, and fewer refusals are

00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:52.651
planned only for Daybreak Red,

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:54.820
which needs stronger verification.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.736
Before you switch,

00:00:56.536 --> 00:00:57.902
run your own evals and

00:00:57.702 --> 00:00:58.874
compare outcomes.

00:00:58.914 --> 00:01:00.854
Direct API calls miss the

00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:02.926
Codex prompt that OpenAI says

00:01:02.726 --> 00:01:05.329
cuts omissions, so make reports

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:06.489
list every error.

00:01:06.529 --> 00:01:09.077
Security teams, plan for refusals.

00:01:09.627 --> 00:01:10.742
The price fell,

00:01:10.542 --> 00:01:12.084
the cyber ceiling rose,

00:01:11.884 --> 00:01:13.059
and the model got a

00:01:12.859 --> 00:01:14.462
little worse at telling you

00:01:14.262 --> 00:01:15.804
when something went wrong.

00:01:16.354 --> 00:01:17.761
Read the full story on

00:01:17.561 --> 00:01:18.499
The Dispatch.

